+## Breakout confirmation (2026-11-11)
+
+Applies to every entry whose case is "price broke a level": a fresh `setup = breakout`, and every WAIT trigger of the form "close above X". It applies to all strategies and to rescued tickers. TURNAROUND keeps its own exemption from rule 3 below.
+
+**Why:**
+- **DECK (2026-11-09) was upgraded WAIT → BUY — REDUCED** on a close only 0.4% above $90.04, on 1.41× volume, below MA200, after three rejections at $90.5–91.7. It fell back below the level the next day.
+- **Test (29,296 first closes above a 60-day high, 780 pipeline tickers, 2015–2026, 15-day return vs SPY):**
+  - Failures (a close back below the level within 5 days) fall steadily as the close clears the level by more: 67% under 0.5% above, 56% at 0.5–1%, 48% at 1–2%, 35% at 2–4%.
+  - Failures also fall with volume: ~60% under 1.2×, 38% over 2×.
+  - Breakouts below MA200 averaged −1.2% vs SPY; DECK-like cases averaged −1.4%, with 73% failing.
+  - Above MA200, ≥ 1% clearance and ≥ 1.5× volume averaged +0.4% vs SPY, with 31% failing.
+- **Literature:**
+  - Brock, Lakonishok & LeBaron (1992) used a 1% band to filter range breakouts.
+  - Osler (2003): stop orders cluster just beyond a level, so a marginal close has not triggered them yet.
+  - Garzarelli et al. (2014) and Chung & Bellotti (2021): each bounce off a level makes the next bounce more likely.
+
+**Rules:**
+1. **Confirmed breakout = both of these:**
+   - a **close ≥ 1% above the level**;
+   - **volume ≥ 1.5×** the 20-day average.
+
+   If only one of the two is met, the trigger has **not** fired yet. Upgrade only after a **second consecutive close above the level**. A marginal first close is never enough to upgrade WAIT → BUY.
+2. **Write triggers in this form:** "close ≥ 1% above X (≥ $Y) on ≥ 1.5× volume, or two consecutive closes above X". Do not write "close > X on ≥ 1.2× volume".
+3. **Breakout below MA200** (SWING / MOMENTUM / POSITION): MA200 is the real ceiling, so measure R:R to MA200, not to a target above it.
+   - If R:R to MA200 is < 1.2, the verdict is **WAIT**, with the trigger "close above MA200 [value]".
+   - A BUY needs R:R to MA200 ≥ 1.2 **and** rule 1 met in full.
+4. **Repeated rejections:** if price has been turned back at the level **3 or more times** in the last 60 sessions, name it in the Adjudication.
+   - Rule 1 then applies with no shortcut: both conditions on one day, or two consecutive closes.
+   - The number of touches is context, not a bull point. More touches make the level stronger, and the test showed no better returns after more touches.
+5. **Failed breakout = bear evidence:** a close back below the level within 5 sessions of a trigger firing. Do not re-issue the same trigger the next day; reset it to the next higher swing high.
+
+**TURNAROUND:** its reversal trigger (condition 1) uses the same confirmation standard when it is a level break, for example "close ≥ 1% above the spring-day high on ≥ 1.5× volume". Rule 3 (MA200) does not apply.
+
